## 8. Questions & Answers

### Q: What is LangServe?

LangServe is a LangChain utility that auto-generates a FastAPI server from your LangChain/LangGraph code with one line. You call `add_routes(app, graph, path="/evaluate")` and it creates `/invoke`, `/stream`, `/batch`, and `/playground` endpoints automatically. Java analogy: like Spring Data REST — define a repository and Spring auto-generates the full CRUD API. We're not using it for Kuber because: (1) limited control over authentication, error handling, and async patterns, (2) auto-generated schemas create an unstable API contract for the Java team, and (3) LangChain now recommends LangSmith Deployment over standalone LangServe for production.

### Q: Why HTTP 202 instead of 200?

HTTP 202 Accepted means "I received your request but haven't processed it yet." This is the correct HTTP semantics for async operations. 200 would imply the evaluation is complete and the body contains the result. Using 202 makes the API contract clear: work is queued, not done.

### Q: What happens if the container crashes during an evaluation?

With BackgroundTasks (development): the evaluation is lost. For production: upgrade to Celery + SQS (task persists in queue, new worker picks it up) or AWS Step Functions (state managed by AWS). LangGraph's Redis checkpointing also helps — resume from last checkpoint on restart.

### Q: How will the Java Loan Service call this API?

Use Spring's WebClient (reactive) or RestTemplate: (1) POST /evaluate, receive 202 + job_id, (2) poll GET /status every 2–3 seconds, (3) when COMPLETE, GET /result. Alternative: implement webhook callback — FastAPI POSTs result back to Loan Service, eliminating polling.

### Q: Why Gunicorn + Uvicorn instead of just Uvicorn?

Uvicorn alone is single-process — handles async well but can't use multiple CPU cores. Gunicorn manages multiple worker processes, each running Uvicorn. This gives process-level isolation (one slow evaluation doesn't block others) plus async I/O within each process. Industry standard for production FastAPI.

